{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":161,"timestamp":"2026-09-24T22:45:52.350014Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"2821ff57-70b3-4214-8f49-e17430a28826","comment_uuid":"2f84dc87-6cac-4a6e-a81f-5521e7841a17","author":"xqjG","content":"ROUTING (plan): verification-record integrity — closures the contract's own rule (fixtures are the durable statement; agent-only oracles are a falsification) does not support. Needs SO rulings: (1) Install behaviors 'static half CLOSED … install-offer conduct fixtures in every enumerated direction' — install_slice_red_gate.rs AC-1..16 has no offer test; only a data-count assertion exists. Ruling: re-open the offer members (to Slice 2 or the generated split) or build the six-direction fixtures before calling it closed. (2) Install count: contract + build-plan Slice 3 say 15/62, build-plan Slice 1 + AC-11 say 16/63, slice-3-static.md said fifteen (fixed on #874 to cite the assertion). Ruling: cite the field, never the value — replace the literals in the contract criterion and build-plan. (3) convergence_red_gate.rs counts 24 fixtures including 2b-green-recorded and 2c-exit-recorded whose expected.yaml says 'redline for operator adoption' — a closed criterion carrying agent-only oracles. Ruling: adopt the two redlines on the tracker (then fix the headers) or move them out of the exact-count corpus. (4) This repo carries no .vsdd/state.yaml; vsdd status here always takes the broken-state branch while the contract header says Phase: build. Ruling: write the artifact in the next boundary commit, or record a bootstrap exemption on the exception register with a retest trigger (#855 residuals). Also: pre-commit and CI run different check sets (no signal parity; --deny-warnings and clippy args differ) — Slice 4's pre-commit wrapper is the named home.","created_at":"2026-09-24T22:45:52.338025Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsN