{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":162,"timestamp":"2026-09-24T22:45:58.072050Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ebaf9ae2-5a5f-45f3-8cbc-37f619b120c0","comment_uuid":"b1c84554-c274-46a7-864d-7eff81deb0ef","author":"xqjG","content":"ROUTING (plan): maintenance, data plumbing; owner Platform Engineer, validator Data Engineer. (1) vsdd-core/src/init.rs deploys eight data sets + four yaml registries to adopters with no schema pairs, no registry-integrity pattern, no routes.yaml/config.yaml — the pair rule and closed world hold only in this repo; add them to the init payload and the install manifest. (2) Retired-term prohibition has two hand-mirrored homes: templates/registry/vocabulary.yaml deprecated_aliases (the shape mdatron cannot read; deployed to adopters with a false 'CI-armed' header) and .mdatron/vocabulary.yaml anti_patterns (the one that fires); membership differs (provenance's eight aliases, four-dimensional convergence have no anti-pattern). Fix: a mirror-pin test (the #724 pattern) that every deprecated alias has an anti-pattern, and correct the header. (3) .mdatron/code-catalogs.yaml says comprehensive: true with 11 codes while canonical-patterns/the binary emit VSDD-E0201..E0212/E0230 — list them or drop the claim. (4) Four versioning conventions; the .md data sets have no data-version field so binding changes ship at an unchanged version. (5) Bundled phase-primer.json/review-entry.json (deployed, tested) diverge from the live .mdatron copies and keep phase-0; add a byte-identity test. (6) canonical-patterns.yaml letter-cluster denylist is read by nothing (the allowlist in .mdatron/vocabulary.yaml fires) — retire or point. (7) review-entry.json + its fixture test carry the retired review-log design; retire under a decision or route it; the contract cites the hallucinated token to the wrong schema (it is in domain-prompt.json).","created_at":"2026-09-24T22:45:58.059566Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAo