{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":164,"timestamp":"2026-09-24T22:54:06.257974Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"25a225df-1907-40db-baa0-7f1086e67d40","comment_uuid":"8d6c4eb9-7c75-4945-938d-809dc5e9f7b3","author":"xqjG","content":"PILOT RESULT (operator launched 2026-09-24T22:51Z; container 63cffba75660, agent E00r-V2sm-…, image ghcr.io/magnificentlycursed/crosslink-agent:nightly, --effort low --budget-usd 2). Outcome: FAILED at the first prompt; the container exited 0 after 32 s with no session, no plan/result comment, no .kickoff-status. PROVEN end to end (preflight members): image pull + start; trust approval (agent already approved, signing enabled); auth via kickoff.env; worktree + feature branch creation; UID remap; Rust toolchain install; crosslink hook init ('Already initialized'). FALSIFIED: the hook payload presence. The tracked .claude/settings.json wires UserPromptSubmit/PreToolUse to $(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/.claude/hooks/*.py, but .claude/hooks/* is gitignored (crosslink-managed payload), so a fresh worktree carries the wiring and not the scripts; the entrypoint's init step saw the workspace as already initialized and did not redeploy them; the wiring failed closed exactly as designed (vsdd-cli #658 message: 'crosslink hook payload missing … restore the crosslink install before proceeding'), blocking every prompt. Secondary, non-fatal: 'this workspace has not been trusted' dropped the two permissions.allow entries (the folder-trust dialog recorded in supplements/claude-code-cli.md); the --allowedTools list on the CLI carried the run past it. Also noted: the worktree branched from chore/874-corpus-rename (HEAD at launch), not main — harmless for a read-only task, worth knowing for real runs. FIX LANE: (1) fork entrypoint should run 'crosslink init --update' (deploys hook payloads) when the workspace's tracked wiring references missing scripts — a magnificentlycursed/crosslink change, draft in chat for the operator; (2) until then the e