{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":166,"timestamp":"2026-09-24T23:19:12.631880Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"25a225df-1907-40db-baa0-7f1086e67d40","comment_uuid":"3ed0f04a-56f7-453b-a47a-254cbe1f241d","author":"xqjG","content":"PILOT RUN 2 (agent-launched under the operator's 'run the pilot again' instruction, 2026-09-24T23:17Z; container d72ef0551fae, agent E00r-UCyB, new nightly image ab9c2abf built from fork develop 29d01852). PROVEN this run, beyond run 1: the entrypoint's crosslink init filled the missing managed files (all eight hooks deployed under .crosslink/integrations/hooks/, settings.json rewired) — the run-1 defect is gone; the predicted side effect occurred (four tracked files dirtied + AGENTS.md/.codex/ created in the agent worktree, entrypoint-caused). FAILED at the next member: authentication. Claude printed 'Not logged in · Please run /login' and the container exited 0 after 34 s. Cause: version skew between the host binary and the image. The host crosslink (0.9.0-beta.1+fe653b40, pre-sync) launched the container the old way — mounting ~/.claude read-only at /host-auth for the kickoff.env token handoff — while the new image's entrypoint no longer reads /host-auth at all: upstream replaced that handoff with 'crosslink container auth login --provider claude' (a per-user, per-provider persisted login that the new kickoff mounts, gated by CROSSLINK_REQUIRE_LOGIN=1 in the entrypoint). The image also fetched no AGENT_ID-specific auth. Neither the old kickoff.env path nor the new login existed for this run. NEXT (operator's acts, both system-state changes): (1) install the develop-built binary (a hub/storage migration may accompany it — upstream added reconciliation and storage-migration commits since fe653b40; check with the release notes before installing); (2) run 'crosslink container auth login --provider claude' once to persist the container login; then relaunch. Retest trigger unchanged: a headless run that reaches 'crosslink session wo